Patch 3012: the tick-locked audio's output follows the level at once when it falls well under the cushion (fast pace; AUDIO_LOCK_FAST=0 turns it off).

Why (test11 field bundles 2026-11-24 + a local two-copy run 2026-11-26): mid-fight choppy sound comes in clusters of 8-11 short concealed gaps
(13-30 ms) in the first second of a run of slow ticks (50-80 ms). The 90 ms cushion is gone after ~3 such ticks, while the slow pace (3009/3010)
needs two 333 ms buckets to engage and then moves at 0.5/s. That slowness was there to keep the pitch steady; with the pitch-preserving stretch
(3011) a quick tempo change no longer moves the pitch.

- lk_slow_burst: a low point under LK_FAST_FROM (0.60) x the cushion engages the fast pace; while engaged (until the low point is back at
  LK_FAST_HOLD = 0.85 x the cushion) the rate is at most 1 - LK_FAST_GAIN (0.6) x (hold - level) / hold, never under AUDIO_LOCK_SLOW_MIN, ramped
  down at LK_FAST_DOWN (3/s); back up at LK_FAST_UP (0.8/s) while the level is under the hold, then at 3/s (review: at 0.8/s the level overshot the
  cushion by up to ~110 ms, extra delay and drops on a 200 ms device); 3009's own engagement keeps LK_SLOW_UP. Only with the stretch (3011) and the
  slow pace on. Normal play never reaches LK_FAST_FROM; a single tick of ~69 ms or more does (a 76 ms hitch dips the rate for a few ticks).
- the "[audio-lock]" line keeps every field and appends "fast pace: N bursts, S s, rate min R, on|off (...)"; the slow pace's time and rate min no
  longer count the fast pace's (with AUDIO_LOCK_FAST=0 the line is 3011's plus the appended fields).
- tests/test_audio_lock_race.c part 8 (virtual time, real output): steady 30 ticks/s unchanged; single 60-150 ms hitches never worse; lumpy slow
  patches and runs of 45-55 ms ticks at least 3x fewer gaps and clusters (measured 84 -> 19 and 104 -> 3); 76 ms hitches every 2-3 s on a 300 ms
  and a 200 ms device (4 -> 1, 29 -> 1 gaps); never more squeezed or dropped blocks, the low point never lastingly over the cushion (+15 ms mean,
  +30 ms peak); the rate never past the ramps or under the floor. Reviewed: D:\jsp-audit\test12\REVIEW-3012.md (finding 1 fixed as tested there).
Output only, like 3007-3011: the blocks mixed, the read index and the notify events are untouched (determinism unchanged).
